+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Foundations
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Add `JsonPatchError`, a private pointer-tokenizer, a prototype-safe deep clone, and `jsonEqual` to `src/index.ts`, with short doc comments citing RFC 6902/6901; verify the module loads under `npm test`
+- [ ] 1.2 Add `applyPatch` skeleton: patch/operation validation (array, object, `op`, `path`, `value`, `from`, unknown `op`), cloning the document, sequential application; verify with the structure scenarios
+
+## 2. Operations
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Implement `add` (object, array insert, `-`, index errors, root, missing/scalar parent, `__proto__`)
+- [ ] 2.2 Implement `remove` and `replace` (existence, array shift, root rules)
+- [ ] 2.3 Implement `move` (post-removal add, same-location no-op, proper-prefix check by token, missing `from`) and `copy` (independent copy)
+- [ ] 2.4 Implement `test` using `jsonEqual` (missing location, type differences, key order)
+
+## 3. Tests
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Add `test/patch.test.ts` with a test for every scenario in specs/json-patch/spec.md (structure, no mutation/aliasing, add, remove, replace, move, copy, test, errors); verify with `npm test`
+- [ ] 3.2 Add the RFC 6902 Appendix A examples A.1–A.16 as tests; verify with `npm test`
+
+## 4. Integration
+
+- [ ] 4.1 Run `npm test` from a clean state and `openspec validate add-json-patch`; verify both succeed
